        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="0741" n="645" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg645"/>

                <head>No. 404.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Bingham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 6,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Referring to Mr. De Long’s dispatch of the 2d of June, No. 415, upon the subject
                    of hunting regulations established by the Japanese government, I have to request
                    you to examine those regulations and to report whether, in your opinion, there
                    is anything contained therein which conflicts with the privileges secured by
                    treaty to American citizens in Japan.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
